# Generated QA artifacts at the qa/ root.
#
# Every test run `capture erase`s and then regenerates these via export()/
# saving()/xlsx() targets, so tracking them produced only binary churn and
# violated the "artifacts never tracked" distribution standard. They are
# recreated on demand by the QA suite, so nothing depends on a tracked copy.
#
# Anchored to the qa/ root with a leading slash. Most crossval suites write
# generated R cross-check CSVs to c(tmpdir); the ZZF oracle deliberately
# regenerates qa/data/ and validates its manifest on every run. None of those
# generated inputs or outputs is a tracked fixture.
/*.dta
/*.xlsx
/*.csv
/*.log
/*.smcl
/data/

# R oracle cache. Every crossval_*_r.R is a pure function of its inputs (fixed
# seeds, or no RNG at all), so its output is a constant; _fg_oracle_cache.R
# caches it keyed on the script + input-file content, the named parameters,
# and the R/package/platform versions. The cache lives OUTSIDE the tree
# ($FG_ORACLE_CACHE_DIR, else ~/.cache/R/finegray_qa) so the devkit's scratch
# copies share it; this pattern only covers a cache pointed back here by hand.
# Never tracked, for the same reason /data/ is not -- and because a cache
# committed from one machine's R build is exactly the oracle drift the
# crossvals exist to catch.  Force a recompute with FG_ORACLE_NOCACHE=1.
/.oracle_cache/
